# .htaccess · r001 · 11 Oct 2026 · role: docroot rewrite · item H54 (Alan, Q2 of 11 Oct 2026: one canonical hostname)
# gpbm.uk serves the application; www.gpbm.uk answers 301 to the same path and query on gpbm.uk.
# The condition names the host, so this file is inert on MountZion (gpbm.local) and on images/files, which
# have their own docroots. The http-to-https 301 is 20i's own, in front of Apache, and is not this file's.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
RewriteEngine On
RewriteCond %{HTTP_HOST} ^www\.gpbm\.uk$ [NC]
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ https://gpbm.uk/$1 [R=301,L]
</IfModule>
